  "problem": "A study shows that for a particular area in a specific season,\n\n- on a day that follows a day without precipitation, there is a $25%$ chance to have rain and a $35%$ chance to have snow.\n\n- on a day that follows a rainy day, there is a $40%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have snow.\n\n- on a day that follows a snowy day, there is a $50%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have rain.\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}a & 0.4 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.25 & b & 0.05 \\\\ 0.35 & 0.05 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
